            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-callout-amber">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">For the 500-jar pilot specifically</p>
        <p>Best path: <strong>request 4 quotes</strong> — from Amigo Sampoorna (Bangalore pickup), Mahalaxmi Industries (Indore MP, has the exact 63mm 250ml spec), Ajanta Bottle (Delhi national), and Myperfectpack (low-MOQ digital). Compare on: per-jar all-in cost (jar + cap + foil), MOQ, lead time, and willingness to ship sample 10–20 jars before bulk PO.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-callout">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">⚠️ Jabalpur is NOT a glass-jar hub</p>
        <p>Despite some online listings + earlier assumption in our own docs, Jabalpur (Civil Lines, Wright Town, Madan Mahal areas) has plastic bottle manufacturers + general packaging traders, but <strong>no dedicated glass-jar factory</strong> for the custom-design + cap + foil-print spec we need. Real glass production in MP is in <strong>Indore (Mahalaxmi Industries)</strong>; the dominant Indian hub overall is <strong>Firozabad, UP</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CAP PRINTING -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">3. Cap manufacturers (with printing capability)</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">For v2 when you add the foil-stamped brand mark on the cap top. Specialist closure companies are better than asking the jar trader to do this.</p>

      <div class="sup-table-wrap">
        <table class="sup-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Location</th><th>Capabilities</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Metal Closures Pvt Ltd</strong></td>
              <td>Kanakapura Road, Bangalore</td>
              <td>Manufactures crown corks, twist-off lug caps, screwcaps, roll-on pilfer-proof caps. <strong>Can print under crowns</strong> for promo offers (so they have print capability).</td>
              <td>✓ <strong>Strong Bangalore pick</strong>. ISO 9001:2008. In business since 1977. Serves food + spices industry.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Ajanta Bottle Pvt Ltd</strong></td>
              <td>Delhi (national)</td>
              <td>Customisable closures with logo + branding. Printing MOQ 5,000 pcs.</td>
              <td>OK for Year 1 scale (1,000+ jars) but printing MOQ doesn't fit pilot</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-callout">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">Pilot v1 vs v2 cap strategy (matches PACKAGING.md §2)</p>
        <p><strong>v1 launch (500 jars)</strong>: plain stock gold tinplate caps from your jar supplier. Zero print cost. Get to market fast.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>v2 (1,000+ jars, post-pilot)</strong>: switch to Metal Closures Pvt Ltd or similar for hot-foil-stamped "MGS" brand mark on the cap top. Tooling: ~₹2,000–5,000 one-time per design. Per-cap print: ₹1–3.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- INDUCTION FOIL + EPE -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">4. Induction foil seals + EPE liners</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Layers 1 + 2 of the 3-layer seal system (see PACKAGING.md §9). Often bundled with cap orders, but specialist suppliers give better rates at scale.</p>

      <div class="sup-table-wrap">
        <table class="sup-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Location</th><th>What they make</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Dolphin Labels</strong></td>
              <td>Bangalore</td>
              <td>Induction sealing wads in 53mm, 63mm, 83mm. Aluminium foil with cardboard. Specialises in PET jar sealing (works for glass too).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Sri Balaji Chemicals</strong></td>
              <td>Nagarabhavi, Bengaluru (560072)</td>
              <td>Induction sealing aluminium foil wads manufacturer. Direct manufacturer.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Security Seal / Security Holograms</strong></td>
              <td>Bapuji Nagar, Bengaluru</td>
              <td>Induction aluminium foil wads + tamper-evidence holograms. Multi-industry (food, pharma, lubricants).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Multipack Labels</strong></td>
              <td>Gujarat (ships pan-India)</td>
              <td>Induction seals, plain wads, <strong>EPE liners</strong> (foam under cap), aluminium foil seal liners. <strong>One of the few specialists for EPE foam</strong>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Action Pack Enterprises</strong></td>
              <td>Bhiwandi (Mumbai)</td>
              <td>Aluminium seal foils for glass bottles + jars, including for pickle + ghee. Also makes the induction sealing machine itself.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Sambhav Foils and Flexibles</strong></td>
