            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="sup-body" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        For a <strong>500-jar pilot</strong>: buy a roll of 1,000 × 63mm aluminium foil wads from any of the Bangalore suppliers above. Per-piece cost ₹1.5–2. EPE liner is usually pre-inserted into the cap by the cap manufacturer (Amigo Sampoorna ships them assembled).
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- LABEL PRINTERS -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">5. Label printers (Bangalore, small-batch friendly)</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">For the wraparound label per LABEL.md spec — bagasse paper, food-safe matte laminate, wash-off adhesive. Low-MOQ printers are essential at pilot scale.</p>

      <div class="sup-table-wrap">
        <table class="sup-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Location</th><th>Specialty</th><th>MOQ</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Kraftix Digital</strong></td>
              <td>Bangalore (ships pan-India)</td>
              <td>Spice + pickle labels, waterproof + food-safe, premium adhesive. Pre-built for pickle jar use case.</td>
              <td><strong>25 pieces</strong> — lowest in market</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Shivambika Creations</strong></td>
              <td>Bengaluru</td>
              <td>Custom stickers for pickle bottles, ghee bottles, oil bottles. Round + glass-bottle specialist.</td>
              <td>Quote-based</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Sahara Labels Private Limited</strong></td>
              <td>Karihobanahalli Peenya, Bengaluru</td>
              <td>Full-service label printing.</td>
              <td>Quote-based (mid-MOQ)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Myperfectpack</strong></td>
              <td>Bengaluru</td>
              <td>Digital printing, no MOQ, multi-product platform.</td>
              <td><strong>NO MOQ</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td colspan="4" style="font-size: 12px; color: rgba(42,26,16,0.6); padding-top: 12px;"><strong>Also in Peenya Industrial Area</strong>: 27+ label manufacturers per Justdial listings — easy to walk in for in-person quotes.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-callout">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">Bagasse paper sourcing — the catch</p>
        <p>LABEL.md specs <strong>sugarcane bagasse paper</strong>. Most small Bangalore printers stock regular synthetic BOPP or matte paper, NOT bagasse. Ask each: "Do you stock <strong>sugarcane bagasse paper</strong> for food labels? If not, can you source it?" Specialty option: <strong>Bhumi Originals</strong> (online, custom prints on bagasse paper, ship pan-India) — already mentioned in LABEL.md.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TAMPER BAND -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">6. Tamper bands (Layer 3 — joint-only band)</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Per PACKAGING.md §9, we're using a 6mm joint band (not a full shrink sleeve). Most label printers can handle the PET shrink film print.</p>

      <ul class="sup-bullets">
        <li>The label printers in Section 5 above (especially <strong>Kraftix</strong>, <strong>Shivambika</strong>, <strong>Myperfectpack</strong>) typically also print PET shrink film for tamper bands. Ask them.</li>
        <li>IndiaMART search term: <em>"PET tamper evident neck band 63mm food grade"</em></li>
        <li>For specialty pre-cut tamper bands: <strong>Multipack Labels (Gujarat)</strong> also stocks tamper bands.</li>
        <li>Cost target: ₹0.50–0.80 per band at 500-jar volume.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- CO-PACKER OPTION -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">7. The "skip manufacturing entirely" option — co-packers</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Once volumes scale past mom's kitchen (or if you want ZERO production hassle), contract pickle production to a licensed manufacturer who handles cook + fill + label under their FSSAI.</p>

      <p class="sup-body">
        <strong>Bangalore + Karnataka has a contract-packaging ecosystem</strong> visible on IndiaMART, TradeIndia, and Justdial. Listings exist for "Packaging Services for Pickles in Bangalore" + "Contract Packaging Services in Bengaluru."
      </p>

      <p class="sup-body" style="margin-top: 12px;">
        <strong>Caveats</strong> at pilot scale:
      </p>
      <ul class="sup-bullets">
        <li>Most listed Bangalore co-packers want MOQs of 1,000+ jars (or kg of finished pickle) per batch — usually too big for the first pilot</li>
        <li>Bidadi industrial belt + Hosakote have small food manufacturers who'll take 500-jar private-label contracts — found via word-of-mouth more than online listings</li>
        <li>Per-jar co-packing cost: <strong>₹30–60 above raw ingredients</strong> at small batch (drops to ₹10–20 at 5,000+ jar volumes)</li>
        <li>Their FSSAI license appears on your label as "Manufactured by [X] for Mother's Gold Spice" — perfectly legal</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="sup-callout-amber">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">When co-packing makes sense</p>
        <p>Not for the first pilot (mom's kitchen is the authentic-recipe story you want to tell). <strong>Revisit at month 6+</strong> when revenue can justify the per-jar cost increase AND mom doesn't have to spend 4–6 hours/day cooking pickle. Discussed in more detail in <a href="/setup" class="sup-link">/setup</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OUTREACH TEMPLATE -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">8. The outreach plan — week 1</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Cold-email or WhatsApp the top 5 suppliers in week 1. By week 2 you'll have 2–3 sample-jar quotes to compare.</p>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink mt-4 mb-3">The 6 suppliers to contact first</h3>
      <ol class="sup-step-list">
        <li><strong>Amigo Sampoorna</strong> (Bangalore, jar+cap kit) — <code>amigosampoorna.in</code> · also search "Amigo Sampoorna Bangalore" on IndiaMART for direct contact number</li>
        <li><strong>Mahalaxmi Industries</strong> (Indore MP, has exact 63mm × 250ml spec) — <code>mahalaxmiindustries.in</code> · Sanwer Road, Sector F Industrial Area, Indore</li>
        <li><strong>Ajanta Bottle</strong> (Delhi national) — <code>ajantabottle.com</code></li>
        <li><strong>Myperfectpack</strong> (Bangalore, no-MOQ) — <code>myperfectpack.com</code></li>
        <li><strong>Kraftix Digital</strong> (Bangalore, labels) — <code>kraftixdigital.in</code></li>
        <li><strong>Metal Closures Pvt Ltd</strong> (Bangalore, caps for v2) — Justdial: "Metal Closures Pvt Ltd Kanakapura Road"</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Email/WhatsApp template (copy-paste ready)</h3>
      <div class="sup-template">
        <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Quote request — 500 × 250g round wide-mouth pickle jars (Bangalore pilot)</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 12px;">Hi [Vendor name],</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 8px;">We're launching a small-batch mango pickle brand from Bangalore (Mother's Gold Spice — mothersgoldspice.com) and looking for quotes on the following for our pilot batch:</p>
        <ul class="sup-template-list">
          <li>Quantity: <strong>500 jars</strong> (Tier A pilot — also quote 1,000 and 5,000 for tier comparison)</li>
          <li>Jar: 250g pickle, round wide-mouth, GPI 63/2030 neck finish, clear flint glass, ~150–180g empty weight</li>
          <li>Cap: tinplate, warm champagne gold (Pantone 871–876C range), matte/satin finish, twist-on, food-safe lacquer rated for mustard oil + acidic contents, PVC-free EPE foam liner pre-inserted</li>
          <li>Foil seal: 63mm aluminium induction foil with heat-seal coating, separate from cap</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 10px;"><strong>Need from you:</strong></p>
        <ul class="sup-template-list">
          <li>Per-piece price for jar / cap / foil at 500, 1,000, 5,000 quantities</li>
          <li>Mold/tooling cost (if any)</li>
          <li>Lead time from PO to delivery</li>
          <li>Sample availability — can you ship <strong>5–10 sample units</strong> before bulk order? (Happy to pay for samples + shipping)</li>
          <li>Food-grade material certifications (IS 14536 for glass, food-grade lacquer cert for cap)</li>
          <li>Whether the cap supplier you work with supports <strong>foil stamping on cap top</strong> (we'll want this in v2)</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Full spec sheet at: <code>mothersgoldspice.com/PACKAGING.md</code> (or available on request as PDF).</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Looking forward to your quote.</p>
        <p>Best,<br/>[Your name]<br/>[Mobile] · [Email]<br/>Mother's Gold Spice</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- DECISION FRAMEWORK -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">9. How to pick — the decision framework</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Once 3 quotes are in, score on these dimensions.</p>

      <div class="sup-table-wrap">
        <table class="sup-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Weight</th><th>What to look for</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Per-jar all-in cost</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>Jar + cap + foil + shipping to Bangalore, ÷ 500. Target ≤ ₹35/jar at pilot scale.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Sample willingness</strong></td><td>25%</td><td>Will they ship 5–10 sample units for a small fee? Non-negotiable — if they won't, walk away.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Food-grade certs</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>IS 14536 / BIS for glass, food-grade lacquer cert for cap inner lining (must be rated for mustard oil + acidic content).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Lead time</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>≤ 21 days PO-to-delivery preferred. Anything over 45 days slows the launch.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Bangalore pickup option</strong></td><td>10%</td><td>Saves ₹3,000–8,000 in inbound shipping for 500-jar order.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Future scalability</strong></td><td>5%</td><td>Can they handle 1,000 → 5,000 → 10,000 jar orders later without dropping you? Ask for their largest current customer.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-callout">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">After quotes come in</p>
        <p>Order <strong>5–10 sample jars from the top 2 suppliers</strong> (don't pick blind from quote alone). Test for:</p>
        <ul class="sup-bullets" style="margin-top: 6px;">
          <li>Cap holds an airtight seal after 1 week with oil + pickle inside</li>
          <li>Jar survives a 1-meter drop test onto wood (acceptable: cap dents, body unbroken)</li>
          <li>Label adheres cleanly to the body panel after 48 hrs (test against a label printer's sample too)</li>
          <li>Foil bonds properly when sealed via induction (need a sealer for this — Layer 2 step in PACKAGING.md §9)</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>Sample order cost: ~₹500–1,500 per supplier</strong>. Cheap insurance against committing 500 jars to a bad batch.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CLOSING -->
